\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 MNI Coordinates Input\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 This folder includes 
\f0\b MNI152_8mm_coord_dyi.mat
\f1\b0 , containing coordinates for the 3559-voxel MNI152 8-mm grid used by the FREQ-NESS example data. Keep one and only one .mat coordinate file in this folder. If your source-reconstructed data use a different source space or voxel ordering, replace the bundled file with your own coordinate file.\
The .mat file must contain 
\f0\b a single variable
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 a matrix named however you prefer (e.g., 
\fs26 MNI8
\fs24 )\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 with size 
\f0\b Nvoxels \'d7 3
\f1\b0 \
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 representing the 
\f0\b MNI coordinates
\f1\b0  (X, Y, Z) of each voxel used in your source-reconstructed data.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Example:
\fs26 \
3559 \'d7 3   double    % one row per voxel, 3 columns for X/Y/Z\

\fs24 The pipeline will automatically load this file and use the voxel coordinates to operate along the 
\f0\b voxel dimension
\f1\b0  and generate spatial visualizations.\
The number of rows and their ordering must match the voxels in every source-reconstructed dataset. If the row count does not match, FREQNESS_Startup will ignore the coordinates and the pipeline will continue without spatial analyses.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

